From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lech Piekarski <isilweo@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 20:43:25 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: apq8053-lenovo-cd-18781y: run the SDHC2 I/O
 supply at 1.8 V

L12 is the vqmmc supply of SDHC2, which carries the QCA9379 WLAN card
over SDIO. Its range of 1.8-2.95 V lets sdhci-msm advertise 3.0 V
signalling (sdhci_msm_set_regulator_caps() sets CORE_3_0V_SUPPORT), so
whenever the host turns the supply on, msm_toggle_vqmmc() first sets it
to the 3.3 V level, which L12 serves at 2.95 V, and the card is only
switched to 1.8 V later during UHS initialization.

The stock DT restricts the SDHC2 I/O supply to 1.8 V
(qcom,vdd-io-voltage-level = <1800000 1800000>). Limit L12 to 1.8 V as
well. L12 has no other consumer. No failure was isolated to the 2.95 V
phase alone.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Assisted-by: Codex:gpt-6.2-astra
Source: https://github.com/isilweo/linux/commit/3ca5b5ccc4d319252ef7f81736a3f8b2eb683405
Base-commit: 1c1a919fd728c881e7ccaf3cf18a3cf3055e0429
